window.HFIDX=[{"id":"home","t":"Seven herbs. Fermented slowly. Born in Hungary. Now in Singapore.","k":"Page","x":"Fermented herbal food supplements Seven herbs. Fermented slowly. Born in Hungary. Now in Singapore. Scroll down. We will show you where it comes from, how it is made, and how it fits into a day. Shop the range How it is made Chapter one · Where it began It started in Hungary, with a scientist and a lot of herbs. A Hungarian founding team, with a scientist at its centre, developed Herbaferm Drops. The Drops were registered in Hungary in 2018. Since 2023, Herbaferm has been a Singapore company. 2018 Drops registered in Hungary 20 + years of research behind the work To confirm 2023 Herbaferm Pte. Ltd. in Singapore Meet the team Chapter two · Seven herbs you probably know Chamomile Matricaria chamomilla A familiar herb in European kitchens and herbal teas, traditionally used for gentle digestive comfort. Yarrow Achillea millefolium A wayside flowering herb used in traditional European herbal practice to support digestion and normal gut function. Elderflower Sambucus nigra The creamy blossoms of the elder tree, a classic ingredient in traditional European preparations. Rosehip Rosa canina The fruit of the dog rose, a natural source of vitamin C and long valued in traditional herbal use. Propolis Apis mellifera propolis A resinous substance collected by bees from plant buds, traditionally used for its natural, protective qualities. Oak bark Quercus robur Contains tannins and has a long tradition of use in herbal preparations for the digestive tract. White wormwood Artemisia absinthium A bitter herb used in traditional European practice to support digestion and maintain a healthy "},{"id":"shop","t":"Shop Herbaferm","k":"Page","x":"Home / Shop The range Shop Herbaferm Three fermented herbal food supplements. Prices in Singapore dollars. Signature product Herbaferm Drops Herbal extract made by natural fermentation, taken in a glass of water. S$55 30 ml, about a month View product Add to cart Everyday add-in Fiber Elite A fibre-rich additive for smoothies, shakes, yoghurt and porridge. S$55 125 g, about a month View product Add to cart Optional add-on Prefer HF400 Capsules of fermented herb fibres, taken alongside Drops. S$45 14 capsules View product Add to cart The whole range Drops, Fiber Elite and Prefer HF400 are made to be used together. Prices in Singapore dollars. Delivery, returns and checkout are connected in the live build. To supply Buy online now The whole range ships from this store. It is also listed on the ConnectingDNA marketplace in Singapore. Clinics and stockists Being built. Leave your email for stockist news. Email address Tell me How long will a bottle last? A 30 ml bottle holds about 480 drops. Move the sliders to match how you take them. Drops per time 8 Times per day 2 30 days from one 30 ml bottle Pick the way you would like to use it \"I want a simple daily routine\" Herbaferm Drops go into a glass of water, morning and evening. The core of the range. Herbaferm Drops \"I would rather add it to meals\" Fiber Elite stirs into smoothies, shakes, yoghurt or porridge, and can be heated. Fiber Elite \"I like capsules\" Prefer HF400 pairs fermented herb fibres with fulvic acid, humic acid and vitamin C. Prefer HF400 The range side by side Herbaferm Drops Fiber Elite Prefer HF400 Format Liq"},{"id":"drops","t":"Herbaferm Drops","k":"Product","x":"Home / Shop / Herbaferm Drops The pack Seven herbs In use Herbaferm Drops A herbal extract made by natural fermentation. Take it in a glass of water, morning and evening. S$55 30 ml, about one month − 1 + Add to cart No preservatives No artificial colours Registered in Hungary, 2018 Seven herbs, naturally fermented Per bottle About 480 drops, S$1.83 a day Regular amount 8 drops, twice a day Storage Fridge, 5 to 12 °C Free from Preservatives Food supplement. Speak to a healthcare professional if you are pregnant or take medication. 8 drops, twice a day 480 drops in a 30 ml bottle 1 month from one bottle S$1.83 a day How to take it 1 Fill a glass About 1.5 dl of water. 2 Add 8 drops Morning and evening. Shake the bottle first. 3 Back in the fridge Keep it at 5 to 12 °C. There are no preservatives. New to it? Start with 5 drops morning and evening and build up over two to three weeks. Read the first-month guide . To confirm Seven herbs, fermented slowly Chamomile, yarrow, elderflower, rosehip, propolis, oak bark and white wormwood. Kitchen and herbal-tea plants from Europe, fermented the traditional way. No artificial additives, preservatives or colours. Meet the seven herbs Details and safety How to use Ingredients Good to know Regular use 8 drops in 1.5 dl of water, twice a day. An occasional range of 5 to 15 drops is acceptable depending on body weight and age. Getting started Start with 5 drops in the morning and 5 in the evening, then increase gradually to up to 15 drops twice a day over two to three weeks. After that, return to 8 drops twice a day. To confirm Storage Kee"},{"id":"fiber","t":"Fiber Elite","k":"Product","x":"Home / Shop / Fiber Elite Fiber Elite A fibre-rich add-in with a malt aroma. Stir it into food and drinks, or heat it. S$55 125 g, about one month − 1 + Add to cart Can be heated and cooked with Vegan and GMO-free, per the leaflet Contains gluten Fine powder, malty aroma Everyday amount 3.5 g a day, about S$1.54 Athletes 3.5 g, 2 to 3 times a day Made from 75% barley malt, 12.5% oat flour Allergens Contains gluten Food supplement. Vegan and GMO-free, according to the leaflet. 3.5 g a day, with a meal 125 g pouch, 35 servings About a month from one pouch S$1.54 a day How to take it 1 Measure 3.5 g A small spoonful of the fine powder. 2 Stir it in Porridge, yoghurt, a smoothie or a protein shake. It can be heated too. 3 On training days 3.5 g two to three times a day, after exercise. Need ideas? Four easy ways to eat Fiber Elite . What is in the pouch 75% whole barley malt and 12.5% oat flour, with a characteristic malt aroma. Contains gluten. To confirm The final composition is still to be confirmed with Herbaferm. A 31-day study in 20 elite water polo players looked at a vegan protein supplement with pre- and probiotics. Herbaferm's founders are among its authors and the abstract does not name Fiber Elite. See the reference Details and safety How to use Ingredients The study Everyday 3.5 g a day, with a meal. After training 3.5 g two to three times a day, preferably stirred into a smoothie or protein shake. Ideas Yoghurt, porridge, smoothies and shakes. Fiber Elite can also be heated, which makes it the one product in the range suited to cooking. See four easy ways to eat i"},{"id":"prefer","t":"Prefer HF400","k":"Product","x":"Home / Shop / Prefer HF400 The pack Close up Prefer HF400 Fermented herb fibre capsules, developed to be taken with Herbaferm Drops. S$45 14 capsules, 400 mg each − 1 + Add to cart Made to go with Drops A one-week trial pack Gelatine capsule Ask first if histamine-sensitive How to take 1 capsule morning and evening Fermented herb fibres 200 mg per capsule Capsule shell Gelatine Price per capsule S$3.21 One 14-capsule pack lasts 7 days at two capsules a day, so it works as a trial pack. Food supplement. Histamine sensitivity: ask a healthcare professional first. 2 capsules a day 14 capsules, one week 200 mg fermented herb fibres each S$3.21 per capsule How to take it 1 Morning One capsule with your glass of water. 2 Evening One more capsule with your second glass. 3 Alongside Drops Prefer HF400 was developed to complement Herbaferm Drops. A 14-capsule pack lasts 7 days, so it works well as a trial. To confirm Another Herbaferm document describes a different dose. What is in one 400 mg capsule 200 mg fermented herb fibres (chamomile, yarrow, rosehip, elderflower, propolis, oak bark, wormwood) 120 mg fulvic acid 51 mg humic acid 29 mg vitamin C Gelatine capsule shell, so not suitable for vegetarians. Halal status is not confirmed yet. To confirm Details and safety How to use Ingredients Good to know Dose 2 capsules a day, one in the morning and one in the evening. With Drops Prefer HF400 was developed to complement Herbaferm Drops, taken morning and evening. Pack 14 capsules is one week at two a day. To confirm Another Herbaferm document describes a different dose. Per 400 mg "},{"id":"ingredients","t":"Seven herbs, one fermentation","k":"Page","x":"Home / Ingredients Ingredients Seven herbs, one fermentation What goes into each product, and what is left out. Chamomile Matricaria chamomilla Yarrow Achillea millefolium Elderflower Sambucus nigra Rosehip Rosa canina Propolis Apis mellifera propolis Oak bark Quercus robur White wormwood Artemisia absinthium Chamomile Matricaria chamomilla A familiar herb in European kitchens and herbal teas, traditionally used for gentle digestive comfort. Herbaferm Drops Prefer HF400 Yarrow Achillea millefolium A wayside flowering herb used in traditional European herbal practice to support digestion and normal gut function. Herbaferm Drops Prefer HF400 Elderflower Sambucus nigra The creamy blossoms of the elder tree, a classic ingredient in traditional European preparations. Herbaferm Drops Prefer HF400 Rosehip Rosa canina The fruit of the dog rose, a natural source of vitamin C and long valued in traditional herbal use. Herbaferm Drops Prefer HF400 Propolis Apis mellifera propolis A resinous substance collected by bees from plant buds, traditionally used for its natural, protective qualities. Herbaferm Drops Prefer HF400 Oak bark Quercus robur Contains tannins and has a long tradition of use in herbal preparations for the digestive tract. Herbaferm Drops Prefer HF400 White wormwood Artemisia absinthium A bitter herb used in traditional European practice to support digestion and maintain a healthy balance. Herbaferm Drops Prefer HF400 What is in each one Herbaferm Drops A fermented extract of all seven herbs, in a 30 ml bottle. No preservatives, no artificial colours. Fiber Elite 75% wh"},{"id":"science","t":"The science, stated plainly","k":"Page","x":"Home / Science Science The science, stated plainly How fermentation works, the terms explained, and the research behind the range, including what each study does and does not cover. Why fermentation Fermentation is one of the oldest food technologies. Herbaferm ferments a blend of herbs with a natural community of microorganisms, so the result carries the plants and the compounds produced during fermentation. The leaflet describes the drops as containing a diverse natural microbiota in low concentrations. No colony count is published, so we do not quote one. What we say, and what we don't Herbaferm products are dietary supplements. Our own leaflets state that no health effects can be attributed to them. They are not medicines, and they do not diagnose, treat or prevent any condition. From herb to bottle Select a step, or let it play. Select Ferment Mature Bottle Seven herbs are chosen for their long history in European herbal use: chamomile, yarrow, elderflower, rosehip, propolis, oak bark and white wormwood. Terms you will see on gut-health labels Definitions follow the international scientific consensus statements from ISAPP, the International Scientific Association for Probiotics and Prebiotics. Microbiome The community of microorganisms living in a particular environment, here the human gut. Probiotic Live microorganisms that, when given in adequate amounts, confer a health benefit on the host (Hill et al., 2014). Prebiotic A substrate that is selectively used by host microorganisms to confer a health benefit (Gibson et al., 2017). Postbiotic A preparation of inanimate "},{"id":"about","t":"A Hungarian formula, in Singapore","k":"Page","x":"Home / About About Herbaferm A Hungarian formula, in Singapore Who we are, where the range comes from, and the documents behind it. A Hungarian formula, now in Singapore Herbaferm develops food supplements by fermenting medicinal herbs with a natural community of microorganisms. The Drops were registered in Hungary in 2018, and the team set up Herbaferm Pte. Ltd. in Singapore in 2023. The founders come from food science, medicine and finance, and the company still works closely with the scientists behind the formula. To confirm From the first registration to Singapore Budapest The company starts in Budapest, Hungary. The investor deck says about eight years before November 2025. To confirm 2018 Herbaferm Drops registered in Hungary, no. 20075/2018. 2023 Herbaferm Pte. Ltd. established in Singapore. 2024 Study related to Fiber Elite published in the Journal of the International Society of Sports Nutrition. 2026 Gold Award at the CIM Hong Kong Bay Area Vitality Living Brand Outstanding Awards. Additional milestones (formula development, UK launch as ReBiotika, first Singapore partners) can be added once confirmed. To confirm People behind Herbaferm TV Thomas Vargoczky Co-founder and CEO ÁB Ádám Bóday Co-founder, scientist DB Dániel Bóday Co-founder, finance SK Szabina Kodela Singapore contact Herbaferm also runs sites for Hungary and the UK . This site is for Singapore. Names and titles are taken from the investor deck. Photos, short bios and confirmation of roles are needed. To supply Principles Natural process Plant ingredients and traditional fermentation, with no artifici"},{"id":"learn","t":"Guides, ingredients and science","k":"Page","x":"Home / Learn Learn Guides, ingredients and science Everything behind the range in one place: how to use it, what is in it and what the research does and does not say. Your first month with Drops Featured guide Your first month with Drops How to ease in, what to expect, and when to settle on your regular amount. Read the guide All Guides Science Kitchen Ingredients Practical So what is fermentation, really? Science So what is fermentation, really? The old kitchen process behind every Herbaferm product, without the jargon. Your first month with Drops Guide Your first month with Drops How to ease in, what to expect, and when to settle on your regular amount. Four easy ways to eat Fiber Elite Kitchen Four easy ways to eat Fiber Elite It smells a bit like malt and survives the stove, so it goes further than a shake. Probiotic, prebiotic, postbiotic: what the words mean Science Probiotic, prebiotic, postbiotic: what the words mean Three look-alike words on gut-health labels, sorted out in plain English. Meet the seven herbs Ingredients Meet the seven herbs Where each one comes from and what people have traditionally done with it. The gut microbiome in plain words Science The gut microbiome in plain words What the word means, what scientists are still working out, and where food and herbs fit in. Why the bottle goes in the fridge Practical Why the bottle goes in the fridge No preservatives means a bit more care. Here is what that looks like day to day. Articles are drafts written from the product leaflets and published research, for Herbaferm to review and extend. To confirm Get t"},{"id":"quality","t":"Quality you can check","k":"Page","x":"Home / Quality Quality and certificates Quality you can check Registrations, lab documents and manufacturing information, with what is still being updated. Paperwork you can check Asian buyers and clinic partners look at documents first, so they live here. Each item becomes a downloadable file once supplied. Items marked as needing an update are not yet ready for public use. On file Product registration Herbaferm Drops, Hungarian National Institute of Pharmacy and Nutrition, no. 20075/2018. On file Capsule certificate of analysis Capsule shell supplier document for Prefer HF400. On file Product leaflets English leaflets for Drops and Prefer HF400, and the Fiber Elite leaflet. Update needed Microbiology declaration A current lab report is being prepared. Ask us for the latest declaration. Update needed ISO 9001:2015 Renewal in progress. The current certificate will be added here once issued. To supply HACCP plan summary The HACCP file received is a scan. A readable summary is needed. To confirm Singapore classification How the products are classified and labelled in Singapore, as confirmed by Herbaferm. To supply Stability and shelf life Stability data and best-before periods for each product. Developed and produced by Herbaferm Kft. Own production The company develops and produces its dietary supplement family at Csömör, Hungary. Cold storage Drops contain no preservatives and need refrigeration at 5 to 12 °C. We plan the supply chain around this. Shelf life Best-before dates are printed on every pack. Typical periods will be listed once confirmed. To confirm Recognition Go"},{"id":"partners","t":"Carry Herbaferm in Singapore","k":"Page","x":"Home / Partners For clinics, retailers and distributors Carry Herbaferm in Singapore Tell us how you would stock or recommend the range, and we will send the evidence pack. Three kinds of partner Clinics and practitioners Longevity clinics and GPs who offer microbiome testing, personalised nutrition or structured protocols, and recommend supplements to their patients. Retailers Specialist health stores and premium retail. Drops need chilled shelves. Fiber Elite and Prefer HF400 suit ambient shelves. Distributors Bulk and regional partners, and marketplace sellers for the ambient products. What partners usually ask for Eight items, in the order partners tend to ask. We assemble them for you on request. Formulation and ingredient documentation Safety and quality-control information Manufacturing standards and batch testing Stability and shelf-life data Microbiological and contaminant testing Regulatory and product classification Available scientific literature Clinical or real-world evidence, where available Medically oriented partners expect more evidence. Items still being updated are listed on the Quality page. Request the evidence pack Your name Organisation Email I am a Clinic or practitioner Retailer Distributor Other Message Request the evidence pack Prototype form: nothing is sent yet. Live contact: szabina@herbafermsg.com To confirm From enquiry to first order Enquire Tell us what you do and who you serve. Review the pack We send the evidence pack and answer questions. Try the range Samples or a trial order. To confirm Onboard Training material, customer guides and a"},{"id":"contact","t":"Get in touch","k":"Page","x":"Home / Contact Contact Get in touch Questions about the range, an order or a partnership. Email szabina@herbafermsg.com To confirm Company Herbaferm Pte. Ltd., Singapore. UEN 202350449W. Office: 10 Anson Road #22-02, International Plaza, Singapore 079903, as shown on the Singapore leaflet. To confirm Opening hours To supply Practitioners and retailers Use the Partners page to request the evidence pack. Send us a message Your name Email Topic A question about a product An order Becoming a partner Something else Message Send message Prototype form: nothing is sent yet."},{"id":"awards","t":"Awards and accolades","k":"Page","x":"Home / Awards Recognition Awards and accolades What Herbaferm has been recognised for, and what is still to be confirmed. 2026 Gold Award, Bay Area Vitality Living Brand Outstanding Award Presented to Herbaferm by the Chartered Institute of Marketing Hong Kong in the Healthy Dietary (Vegetarian) category for 2025/26. 2026 TOP 10 Winner, TOP 10 Longevity Breakthrough Awards Awarded to Herbaferm Pte. Ltd. by the Asia-Pacific Longevity Medicine Society, in celebration of excellence and innovation in longevity medicine. This recognises the company and its work. It is not evidence that a product works or is safe for any health purpose. Also on the record These are registrations and publications, not awards, but they are part of the same story. Registered in Hungary, 2018 Herbaferm Drops, no. 20075/2018, as a food supplement. Quality and documents Published research, 2024 A study related to Fiber Elite in the Journal of the International Society of Sports Nutrition. What it covers Singapore company, 2023 Herbaferm Pte. Ltd. established in Singapore. About Herbaferm Book, 2026 The Holistic Microbiome: Nature is complex but never complicated By Adam Boday, published by Herbaferm. A plain-language book on the microbiome and the natural world around it. Where to buy it in Singapore is still to be confirmed. To confirm Read our short guide to the gut microbiome Awards recognise the brand. They are not health claims, and our leaflets state that no health effects can be attributed to the products."},{"id":"a-ferment","t":"So what is fermentation, really?","k":"Guide","x":"Home / Learn / Science Science So what is fermentation, really? The old kitchen process behind every Herbaferm product, without the jargon. 1 min read Draft for Herbaferm review If you have ever eaten yoghurt, sourdough, kimchi or miso, you have already met fermentation. Tiny organisms like bacteria and yeasts feed on parts of the food and turn them into something new. That is why yoghurt is tangy and why dough rises. People have been doing this for thousands of years, long before anyone knew what a microbe was. Where the herbs come in Herbaferm takes the same idea and applies it to plants. Chamomile, yarrow, elderflower, rosehip, propolis, oak bark and white wormwood are fermented slowly with a natural community of microorganisms. The leaflet says it is mainly Lactobacillus , at low concentrations. What comes out the other end is a concentrated herbal extract, which is what fills the 30 ml bottle. What we can and cannot tell you We can tell you how the drops are made. We cannot give you a colony count, because there is no verified figure to quote, so we do not quote one. And we do not say the drops treat or prevent anything: they are food supplements, and our own leaflets state that no health effects can be attributed to them. If you like the detail, the Science page lists the studies and what each one does and does not cover. Previous Why the bottle goes in the fridge Next Your first month with Drops"},{"id":"a-month","t":"Your first month with Drops","k":"Guide","x":"Home / Learn / Guide Guide Your first month with Drops How to ease in, what to expect, and when to settle on your regular amount. 1 min read Draft for Herbaferm review A new routine sticks best when it is small and attached to something you already do. For most people that means the glass of water at breakfast. Here is how the leaflet suggests you begin. Days one to three: keep it light Put 5 drops in a glass of water in the morning, and 5 more in the evening. That is all. The bottle lives in the fridge (5 to 12 °C), because the drops have no preservatives. Weeks one to three: go up slowly Add a drop or two every few days, up to a ceiling of 15 drops twice a day. Some people notice a bit of gas or looser stools while their body gets used to it. If that is you, stay where you are, or step back one level. There is no prize for getting there faster. From week three: your regular amount Settle at 8 drops twice a day in about 1.5 dl of water. A 30 ml bottle holds roughly 480 drops, so at that amount it lasts about a month. Before you start If you take medication, are pregnant or have a diagnosed condition, talk to your doctor or pharmacist first. Stop if you react to any ingredient. The Singapore label may be worded a little differently, so go by the pack in your hand. Previous So what is fermentation, really? Next Four easy ways to eat Fiber Elite"},{"id":"a-fiber","t":"Four easy ways to eat Fiber Elite","k":"Guide","x":"Home / Learn / Kitchen Kitchen Four easy ways to eat Fiber Elite It smells a bit like malt and survives the stove, so it goes further than a shake. 1 min read Draft for Herbaferm review Fiber Elite is a fine, flour-like powder with a malty smell, a bit like the inside of a granola bar. The everyday amount on the leaflet is 3.5 g, which is a small spoonful, taken with a meal. Because you can heat it, it is not just for cold drinks. Stirred into porridge Add it near the end of cooking so it blends in, then top with fruit and seeds. In a post-training shake People who train hard take 3.5 g two or three times a day after exercise. Blend it into a protein shake or a smoothie. In a fruit smoothie Banana, berries, your usual milk and a spoonful of Fiber Elite. Nothing fancy. On yoghurt Mix it into plain yoghurt, then add nuts and a drizzle of honey. Worth knowing: Fiber Elite is 75% whole barley malt and 12.5% oat flour, and it contains gluten. These are draft ideas that Herbaferm should test and approve. Previous Your first month with Drops Next Probiotic, prebiotic, postbiotic: what the words mean"},{"id":"a-labels","t":"Probiotic, prebiotic, postbiotic: what the words mean","k":"Guide","x":"Home / Learn / Science Science Probiotic, prebiotic, postbiotic: what the words mean Three look-alike words on gut-health labels, sorted out in plain English. 1 min read Draft for Herbaferm review Walk down any supplement aisle and you will see all three words. They sound alike, but they mean different things. Scientists at ISAPP, the International Scientific Association for Probiotics and Prebiotics, have agreed definitions, and they are worth knowing. Probiotic: the living bugs These are live microorganisms. The definition adds that they must be given in a large enough amount to actually do something for the person taking them. Prebiotic: the food for the bugs This is something the microorganisms already living in your gut use as fuel. It is not a microbe itself. Postbiotic: what is left of the bugs These are microorganisms that are no longer alive, plus the parts and compounds they leave behind. So which is Herbaferm? Herbaferm leaflets use the words \"rebiotic\" and \"prebiotic\". Which category fits on a Singapore label has not been confirmed, so for now we do not call any product a probiotic. The exact definitions and their sources are on the Science page . Previous Four easy ways to eat Fiber Elite Next Meet the seven herbs"},{"id":"a-herbs","t":"Meet the seven herbs","k":"Guide","x":"Home / Learn / Ingredients Ingredients Meet the seven herbs Where each one comes from and what people have traditionally done with it. 1 min read Draft for Herbaferm review On this page Chamomile Yarrow Elderflower Rosehip Propolis Oak bark White wormwood None of these seven is exotic. All of them have a place in European kitchens and herbal cabinets, and that is the point. What is described below is traditional use, not a health effect. Chamomile The little daisy-like flower in the tea you reach for when your stomach is unsettled. Traditionally used for gentle digestive comfort. Yarrow It grows at the edge of fields and paths. Herbal practice in Europe has long used it to support digestion. Elderflower The creamy blossoms of the elder tree, familiar from cordials and traditional preparations. Rosehip The bright fruit of the dog rose, a natural source of vitamin C. Propolis A sticky resin that bees gather from plant buds and use to seal the hive. Valued traditionally for its protective qualities. Oak bark Rich in tannins, which is what gives it its dry, grippy taste. It has a long history in preparations for the digestive tract. White wormwood A very bitter herb. Traditional European practice uses bitter herbs to support digestion. The Ingredients page lets you tap through each herb and see which products use it. Previous Probiotic, prebiotic, postbiotic: what the words mean Next The gut microbiome in plain words"},{"id":"a-gut","t":"The gut microbiome in plain words","k":"Guide","x":"Home / Learn / Science Science The gut microbiome in plain words What the word means, what scientists are still working out, and where food and herbs fit in. 1 min read Draft for Herbaferm review You may have seen the word microbiome on a label or in a headline. It means the community of microorganisms, mostly bacteria, that live in and on the human body. The biggest community is in the gut. A community, not a single thing Everyone carries their own mix, and the mix changes over time with age, food, sleep, medicines and where we live. Researchers are still working out what a healthy mix looks like, and how much any single food or supplement changes it. Why food comes up so often What we eat is one of the everyday things that feeds this community. Fibre-rich plant foods, fermented foods and a varied diet are the usual starting points in general dietary advice. Herbaferm products are food supplements that sit next to a varied diet. They do not replace it. Where Herbaferm fits Herbaferm Drops are made from seven herbs that are fermented slowly with a natural community of microorganisms, and Fiber Elite is a fibre-rich food additive. Our leaflets state that no health effects can be attributed to the products, and we do not claim that they treat or prevent any condition. Want to read more? The Herbaferm team has published a book on the subject, The Holistic Microbiome by Adam Boday. See the About page for details. If you have a digestive condition or take medication, talk to a doctor or pharmacist first. Previous Meet the seven herbs Next Why the bottle goes in the fridge"},{"id":"a-fridge","t":"Why the bottle goes in the fridge","k":"Guide","x":"Home / Learn / Practical Practical Why the bottle goes in the fridge No preservatives means a bit more care. Here is what that looks like day to day. 1 min read Draft for Herbaferm review Herbaferm Drops contain no preservatives. For many people that is the whole appeal. The trade-off is simple: once the bottle is yours, it lives in the fridge, at 5 to 12 °C. At home Keep it in the door shelf, next to the water you pour your morning glass from. Seeing the bottle when you reach for the water is the easiest reminder there is. If you run a clinic or a shop Drops need chilled storage, so they suit a clinic fridge or a chilled shelf better than an ambient display. Fiber Elite and Prefer HF400 are easier: they can sit on a normal shelf. We are happy to talk through storage and delivery with partners. Check the date The best-before date is printed on each pack. Typical shelf-life periods will be added here once they are confirmed. Previous The gut microbiome in plain words Next So what is fermentation, really?"},{"id":"faq","t":"How long does one bottle of Drops last?","k":"Question","x":"A 30 ml bottle holds about 480 drops. At 8 drops twice a day, that is about one month. The leaflet suggests a slower build-up over the first weeks.","q":"How long does one bottle of Drops last?"},{"id":"faq","t":"How do I start with Drops?","k":"Question","x":"The leaflet suggests starting with 5 drops in the morning and 5 in the evening, then increasing gradually to up to 15 drops twice a day over two to three weeks. After that, 8 drops twice a day is the regular amount. Always take the drops in water. To confirm","q":"How do I start with Drops?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Will I notice anything in the first days?","k":"Question","x":"Some people notice temporary digestive changes such as gas or looser stools when they start. This is why we suggest building up gradually. If you are uncomfortable, reduce the amount or pause. To confirm","q":"Will I notice anything in the first days?"},{"id":"faq","t":"How do I use Fiber Elite?","k":"Question","x":"The everyday amount is 3.5 g a day with a meal. Athletes take 3.5 g two to three times a day, after training, ideally in a smoothie or protein shake. You can also stir it into yoghurt or porridge, or heat it into food.","q":"How do I use Fiber Elite?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Can I take the capsules and the drops together?","k":"Question","x":"Yes. Prefer HF400 was developed to be taken together with Herbaferm Drops. The capsule leaflet suggests one capsule in the morning and one in the evening.","q":"Can I take the capsules and the drops together?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Who should speak to a professional first?","k":"Question","x":"Anyone with a diagnosed health condition, anyone taking medication, and anyone who is pregnant. The leaflets also advise stopping the product if you notice hypersensitivity to an ingredient, and using Prefer HF400 only under professional supervision if you have histamine sensitivity.","q":"Who should speak to a professional first?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Are Herbaferm products medicines?","k":"Question","x":"No. They are food supplements. Our leaflets state that no health effects can be attributed to them. They are not intended to diagnose, treat, cure or prevent any disease.","q":"Are Herbaferm products medicines?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Can children use these products?","k":"Question","x":"Speak to a healthcare professional before giving any supplement to a child. To confirm","q":"Can children use these products?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Is Fiber Elite gluten-free?","k":"Question","x":"No. The current leaflet lists 75% whole barley malt and 12.5% oat flour and states that Fiber Elite contains gluten.","q":"Is Fiber Elite gluten-free?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Are the capsules vegetarian or halal?","k":"Question","x":"The capsule shell is gelatine, so the capsules are not suitable for vegetarians. Halal status has not been confirmed. To confirm","q":"Are the capsules vegetarian or halal?"},{"id":"faq","t":"How long do the products keep?","k":"Question","x":"Herbaferm's notes give about 6 months for Drops and about 1 year for the capsules. The best-before date is printed on each pack. To confirm","q":"How long do the products keep?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Are Drops free from alcohol and sugar?","k":"Question","x":"Herbaferm describes the Drops as free from preservatives, alcohol and sugar. The leaflets confirm no preservatives. To confirm","q":"Are Drops free from alcohol and sugar?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Is Herbaferm sold in Singapore yet?","k":"Question","x":"Yes, early on. All three products are listed on the ConnectingDNA marketplace in Singapore, with first sales (12+, 17+ and 20+ units shown at the time of checking). Clinic and retail stockists are still being built. To confirm","q":"Is Herbaferm sold in Singapore yet?"},{"id":"faq","t":"What are the products free from?","k":"Question","x":"The ConnectingDNA listings show a free-from icon set (gluten, sugar, alcohol and lactose free, vegetarian) on all three products. That conflicts with the leaflet, which says Fiber Elite contains gluten, so please rely on the pack label. To confirm","q":"What are the products free from?"},{"id":"faq","t":"What does a day cost?","k":"Question","x":"At list price, Drops at the regular amount are about S$1.83 a day (S$55 for about 30 days). Fiber Elite at 3.5 g a day is about S$1.54 a day. Prefer HF400 is S$3.21 per capsule. Prices are before any offers.","q":"What does a day cost?"},{"id":"faq","t":"How should I store Herbaferm Drops?","k":"Question","x":"Keep the bottle in the fridge at 5 to 12 °C. The drops contain no preservatives. Check the best-before date printed on the pack.","q":"How should I store Herbaferm Drops?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Where are the products made?","k":"Question","x":"Herbaferm Kft. develops and produces the range at Csömör, Hungary. Drops are registered in Hungary under number 20075/2018 as a food supplement.","q":"Where are the products made?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Is Herbaferm approved by the HSA?","k":"Question","x":"In Singapore, health supplements do not need pre-market approval from the Health Sciences Authority, so no supplement can be described as \"HSA approved\". Herbaferm products are marketed as food supplements. To confirm","q":"Is Herbaferm approved by the HSA?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Where can I buy Herbaferm in Singapore?","k":"Question","x":"Today the range is sold through this website and on the ConnectingDNA marketplace. Clinic, pharmacy and retail stockists are being built, and the Shop page has a sign-up for stockist news. To confirm","q":"Where can I buy Herbaferm in Singapore?"},{"id":"faq","t":"How much does delivery cost, and how long does it take?","k":"Question","x":"Delivery details for Singapore will be listed here. To supply","q":"How much does delivery cost, and how long does it take?"},{"id":"faq","t":"What is your returns policy?","k":"Question","x":"Returns and refund terms will be listed here. To supply","q":"What is your returns policy?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Which payment methods do you accept?","k":"Question","x":"The current store accepts major cards and wallets. The live list will be shown here. To confirm","q":"Which payment methods do you accept?"},{"id":"faq","t":"How can my clinic or shop stock Herbaferm?","k":"Question","x":"Send us an enquiry on the Partners page. We reply with the partner evidence pack: formulation, quality and safety information, testing, shelf life and available literature.","q":"How can my clinic or shop stock Herbaferm?"},{"id":"faq","t":"Do you offer samples for practitioners?","k":"Question","x":"Sample availability for practitioners and retail buyers will be confirmed. To confirm","q":"Do you offer samples for practitioners?"}];
